{
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "scope": "user",
  "platforms": [
    "linux"
  ],
  "name": "Steam",
  "description": "Steam, the whole thing. The store without an account: search, a game's details and price, what's on sale and until when, patch notes, Workshop mods, and whether a game runs on Linux (native, Steam Deck and SteamOS ratings, ProtonDB's community tier). The user's account: the wishlist with sale prices (no key needed), and with a free Steam Web API key the library with play time and the never-played backlog, achievements, which friends are online and playing what, and the games the user and friends all own. This computer: installed games and their sizes, download progress, and starting, installing or uninstalling a game through Steam's own windows. It never buys anything.",
  "summary": "Steam store, sales, wishlist, library, achievements, friends and Workshop, plus Linux compatibility (Steam Deck, ProtonDB) and the games on this computer: install, play, uninstall and download progress through Steam's own windows. Never buys. Python standard library only.",
  "keywords": [
    "steam",
    "games",
    "gaming",
    "video games",
    "steam sale",
    "game deals",
    "wishlist",
    "game library",
    "playtime",
    "backlog",
    "achievements",
    "steam friends",
    "who is playing",
    "multiplayer",
    "co-op",
    "steam workshop",
    "mods",
    "patch notes",
    "proton",
    "protondb",
    "steam deck",
    "linux gaming",
    "install game",
    "play game",
    "uninstall game",
    "download progress"
  ],
  "homepage": "https://github.com/JarvisOSLinux/mcp-registry",
  "transports": [
    {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "python3",
      "args": [
        "server.py"
      ],
      "platforms": [
        "linux",
        "darwin"
      ],
      "description": "Steam MCP Server (POSIX)"
    },
    {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "python",
      "args": [
        "server.py"
      ],
      "platforms": [
        "windows"
      ],
      "description": "Steam MCP Server (Windows; python.exe, not python3)"
    }
  ],
  "source": {
    "type": "git",
    "url": "https://github.com/JarvisOSLinux/mcp-registry.git",
    "rev": "43e644a3a95686e5be916b7c4c28d1359c8993a0",
    "path": "servers/steam"
  },
  "setupScript": "setup.sh",
  "setupScriptWindows": "setup.ps1",
  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "search_store",
      "description": "Search the Steam store by name or words: price, discount, native Linux",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "game_details",
      "description": "A game's store details: description, price, release, genres, features, platforms, storage, players now, installed here or not",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "linux_compatibility",
      "description": "Whether a game runs on Linux: native version, Steam Deck and SteamOS ratings, ProtonDB tier, a verdict",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "store_highlights",
      "description": "The store front: current sales with end dates, top sellers, new releases, coming soon",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "game_news",
      "description": "A game's latest patch notes and developer announcements on Steam",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "search_workshop",
      "description": "Find Workshop mods for a game: popular, recent, trending or by search words",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "my_library",
      "description": "The user's Steam games with play time, last played and the never-played backlog",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "achievements",
      "description": "The user's achievements in a game: unlocked, latest, easiest still locked",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "my_wishlist",
      "description": "The user's wishlist with current prices, discounts and sale end dates",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "friends",
      "description": "The user's Steam friends: who is online, their status and what each is playing",
      "threat_level": "elevated"
    },
    {
      "name": "games_in_common",
      "description": "Games the user and named friends all own, multiplayer and co-op first",
      "threat_level": "elevated"
    },
    {
      "name": "installed_games",
      "description": "Games installed on this computer with size, last played and status, and free space per library",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "downloads",
      "description": "What Steam is downloading or updating here, with progress",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "install_game",
      "description": "Install an owned or free game: checks ownership and disk space, opens Steam's install window, then follows the download until it is installed or cancelled, with progress in each reminder",
      "threat_level": "safe",
      "blocking": true,
      "suggestedRemindAfter": 120
    },
    {
      "name": "play_game",
      "description": "Start an installed game through Steam",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "uninstall_game",
      "description": "Uninstall a game through Steam, or cancel its download; says whether Steam removed it or is asking to confirm, and warns when saves aren't in Steam Cloud",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    },
    {
      "name": "open_steam_page",
      "description": "Show a game's store, community or Workshop page, or one Workshop item, in Steam",
      "threat_level": "safe"
    }
  ],
  "configurableProperties": [
    {
      "key": "STEAM_API_KEY",
      "label": "Steam Web API key",
      "description": "Optional; needed for your library, achievements, friends and the Workshop (the store, news, Linux checks, your wishlist and the games on this computer work without it). Get one free at https://steamcommunity.com/dev/apikey: sign in, type any domain name (e.g. localhost) and agree. Steam gives keys only to accounts that have spent at least 5 USD. The key reads what your profile shows publicly.",
      "sensitive": true,
      "required": false
    },
    {
      "key": "STEAM_ID",
      "label": "Steam profile",
      "description": "Optional. Your SteamID64, profile link, or custom URL name. Empty: the account last signed in to Steam on this computer.",
      "sensitive": false,
      "required": false
    },
    {
      "key": "STEAM_COUNTRY",
      "label": "Store country",
      "description": "Optional. Two-letter country code for prices and sales (e.g. US, DE, TR). Empty: from the system locale, else US.",
      "sensitive": false,
      "required": false
    },
    {
      "key": "STEAM_PATH",
      "label": "Steam folder",
      "description": "Optional. Where Steam is installed, if not in the usual place (~/.local/share/Steam, ~/.steam/steam, Flatpak or Snap).",
      "sensitive": false,
      "required": false
    }
  ],
  "trust": {
    "reviewReferences": [
      "https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/webapi_overview",
      "https://steamcommunity.com/dev/apiterms",
      "https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Steam_browser_protocol",
      "https://github.com/JarvisOSLinux/mcp-registry/tree/main/servers/steam"
    ],
    "checks": [
      "license: server code is first-party, under this repository's licence",
      "source: maintained in-tree at servers/steam, pinned by commit",
      "dependencies: none \u2014 Python standard library only (urllib, json, subprocess, shutil)",
      "network: outbound HTTPS to store.steampowered.com, api.steampowered.com and www.protondb.com only; redirects to any other host are refused",
      "credentials: an optional Steam Web API key from the server's settings, sent only to api.steampowered.com and scrubbed from every reply and error",
      "filesystem: reads Steam's own files (libraryfolders.vdf, appmanifest_*.acf, loginusers.vdf for the SteamID only; the login name is never read out); a response cache at $XDG_CACHE_HOME/jarvis-steam, owner-only",
      "processes: install, play, uninstall and open_steam_page hand a steam:// link to xdg-open (or steam), detached, with no output on the MCP wire"
    ],
    "notes": "First-party server maintained in this repository. Store, news, wishlist and Linux data need no account; the library, achievements, friends and Workshop use the user's own Steam Web API key, which returns only what the profile shows publicly, so private profiles are explained, never worked around. The store endpoints (storesearch, appdetails, featuredcategories) are undocumented but public and rate-limited to roughly 200 requests in 5 minutes, so responses are cached. ProtonDB's summaries are its public community data, credited in every result.",
    "securityNotes": "Reads are safe: the Web API only returns what the user's profile already shows publicly, and nothing changes. friends and games_in_common are elevated: they read other people's activity, and friends' names are chosen by them (third-party text, a prompt-injection surface, marked as data in every result). install_game, play_game and uninstall_game are safe by the maintainer's decision (2026-11-23): Steam does the work through its own client and windows, where the user presses Install, and the result says what Steam did. uninstall_game can remove a download in progress without Steam asking, and a game without Steam Cloud can take its saves with it; the result warns when that is the case. No tool can buy anything: install_game refuses a game the user doesn't own unless it is free. Game descriptions, news and Workshop text are written by publishers and mod authors and are marked as data."
  },
